  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></math> is projected at an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with horizontal with a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. After <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> explosion takes place and the particle is broken into two equal pieces. As a result of the explosion, one part comes to rest. The maximum height attained by the other part is (Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)"
